// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
// Reflection that runs (issue #53 Scope A): the module home of the four
// reflected intrinsics -- `@type_name`, `@type_size`, `@field_count`,
// `@field_offset` -- the compiler evaluates directly. Nothing is declared
// here yet on purpose: each intrinsic is an `@`-spelling the C++ backend and
// the self-host stage fold from their own tables into a constant at the call
// site, so an import would add a name to resolve to nothing. A name compiles
// to an ordinary string literal and a measure to an ordinary integer
// constant; there is no runtime walk and no metadata blob.
//
// HOW A FACT IS ASKED FOR. The argument is a type's NAME, written where a
// type belongs (`@type_size(Point)`), the same contextual reading
// `@implements` gets for its struct argument. `@field_offset` takes the
// field LITERAL: only the backend fold can read a name at compile time, so
// a run-time string cannot name a field and no wrapper can step in front
// of these four.
//
// WHAT IT ANSWERS. A struct's name comes from its declaration and a scalar's
// from the spelling written (`@type_name(long)` is `long`). Sizes and offsets
// are the layout model's (`long` is 8, `Point{int, long}` has `y` at 8 and
// is 16 wide). Counts and measures answer `int` -- a count and a byte
// measure are not layout widths (`size_of` in the layout component returns
// `uint`; that is the component API's rounding, and this surface deliberately
// did not copy it). An alias answers what it aliases (C++ answer; the stage
// names no type for one yet -- the parity pin comes with the stage sweep).
//
// Boundaries, stated here so a caller is not surprised by a backend refusal:
//   * A payloaded enum carries MEMBERS, not fields, so all four refuse on
//     one; the member ops come with `enum_from!` (issue #53 Scope B). A
//     payloadless enum is its tagged-union tag on this model -- an `int` --
//     and answers size 4 with field count 0, which is what the
//     representation is.
//   * An interface reference is a fat value `{data, vtable}`, and its
//     reflected facts wait for those two words to have an owning answer.
//   * A type parameter names no layout inside one erased body (`fun
//     tp_size<T>() { return @type_size(T); }` folds `Point` at the call's
//     turbofish on the C++ side and refuses by name on the stage side,
//     which keeps one body); the wrapper route is the shape that landed
//     (derive.fin's bodiless declaration from Scope B; the stage refuses
//     the in-body `T` spelling the same way).
//   * `fields_of` exists as a concept in the issue and is NOT shipped: the
//     field list materializes only when a runtime `FieldInfo` has an owner
//     for its string (Phase B). `@field_offset` and `@field_count` are what
//     composes a walk today.

namespace std {

}
